// Style guide section: Typography
// Markup ported word for word from the original case-study.html.
---
<section class="section_style-guide-type" data-pane="style-guide" id="sg-type">
      <div class="section-frame"><div class="section-card">
        <div class="padding-global padding-section-medium"><div class="container-large">
          <div class="heading_component is-narrow" data-anim=""><span class="text-style-eyebrow text-color-brand">02</span><h2 class="heading-style-h3">Typography</h2><p class="text-color-secondary">Figtree from Google Fonts in 4 weights, with tight tracking on every heading. Sizes shown as desktop / tablet / mobile.</p></div>
          <div class="style-guide_font" data-anim="">
            <p class="style-guide_font-sample">Aa</p>
            <div class="style-guide_font-info"><p class="heading-style-h4">Figtree</p><p class="text-color-secondary">Regular 400 · Medium 500 · Semibold 600 · Bold 700</p><p class="style-guide_code">body: 1.125rem / 1.5, letter-spacing -0.02em, color #0a0a0a</p></div>
          </div>
          <div class="style-guide_subheading" data-anim=""><p class="heading-style-h4">Tag styles</p><p class="text-size-small text-color-secondary">The tag sets the SEO level and the class sets the look, so an h2 can look like an H3 when the layout asks for it. Every heading on these pages has a heading-style class, and the tag styles below are the base for any heading added without one.</p></div>
